            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous dissection of the left main coronary artery treated with percutaneous coronary stenting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E218-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous coronary artery dissection is a rare and often fatal cause of acute myocardial ischemia occurring predominantly in young or middle-aged and otherwise healthy patients. We report a case of spontaneous dissection of the left main coronary artery in a young woman who was successfully treated with percutaneous coronary stent implantation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
